# Never commit a secret. `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` is read from the environment by
# lib/jev.js, and the convenient way to set it locally is a `.env` file — which is
# exactly the kind of file that ends up in a commit by accident.
#
# This matters more than usual here: two TypeSafe/Vercel keys were already leaked in
# plaintext during this project's earlier command-gate attempt, precisely because a
# key pasted into a note is indistinguishable from a key pasted into config.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local logs and analysis output. These contain excerpts of the user's own prompts
# (the ground-truth backfill), so they are not shareable by default.
*.jsonl
!test/fixtures/*.json
assessments*.json
analysis*.json

# Scratch and OS noise.
node_modules/
*.log
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# The probes are diagnostics tied to one machine's DSH install; they are kept in the
# tree deliberately (they document how the real contracts were verified) but their
# captured output is not.
tools/_probe-*.out
